## Result — `falsifier_not_triggered` (6/6 checks)
The three schemes published as methodologically independent (`lffd`, `cnfd`, `cnfem`) are **2 distinct spatial operators × 2 time integrators, covering 3 of the 4 cells** of that design:

| measurement | value |
|---|---|
| `lffd` vs `cnfd` spatial operator | **identical** (attr diff `0.0`; one-step identities 3.7e-16 / 7.8e-16) |
| FEM vs FD distinctness (central-row Nyquist λ ratio) | **3.000000000000000** at every dr (dev ≤ 1.9e-16) |
| FEM vs FD low-mode difference order (smooth mode / Rayleigh) | **2.0000 / 2.0000** |
| published 4-rung orders reproduced | **abs delta 0.0** (lffd 1.9966248643, cnfd 1.9953510344, cnfem 1.9888598802) |
| missing cell `femlf` (FEM+leapfrog), new here | mixed **2.001045**, isolated spatial **1.999993**, monotone/in band |
| isolated spatial order, all 4 cells | 1.9991 / 2.0007 / 2.0005 / 2.0000 |

**Consequence:** "independence holds along spatial discretisation" holds at multiplicity **2, not 3** (`lffd`/`cnfd` share the 3-point FD operator; only the time integrator differs). The order-2 result is *strengthened*: the completed 2×2 design is in band in all four cells.

**Falsifier (ran clean):** false if (a) lffd/cnfd operators differ, (b) FEM≈FD at grid scale or not both 2nd-order at low modes, (c) extraction/code-path/exactness checks fail, (d) any cell leaves |p−2|≤0.3 or loses monotonicity, (e) published cells not reproduced <1e-9.

